From 8d59d57b64626d474c8e2e509c1edd7977742c29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ONYX <onyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:07:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] dzn: avoid invalid calls the Xbox runtime removes the
 device for

- Without relaxed format casting, views outside the resource's typeless
  family (Azahar binds an R32_UINT storage view of a mutable RGBA8 image)
  are invalid; write a null descriptor of the same shape instead.
- Lower sampling of integer textures to texel fetches (D3D12 can't sample
  them; the validator refuses it and signing it is undefined behaviour).
- Convert integer border colours to floats when CreateSampler2 is missing.
- Don't put DENY_SHADER_RESOURCE on the buffer used to map memory.
---
 src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c     |  4 +-
 src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_descriptor_set.c | 88 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c         |  3 +-
 src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_pipeline.c       | 20 ++++++
 src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_private.h        |  4 ++
 5 files changed, 114 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c
